+# Historical native parity review and port record
+
+This is a source-preservation summary of PR 8037 head
+`9ae85474d22ed4a987508293b60bed48f9108a43`, not a current review verdict.
+The original `.claude/science/physics-loops/native-parity-entangler-20260908/`
+packet contained `HANDOFF.md`, `NO_GO_LEDGER.md`, and
+`evidence/native-parity-entangler-cold-review/REVIEW.md`.
+
+The historical handoff reported independent exact and root canonical review,
+followed by integration of main `8257bddfc9`. It explicitly left combined
+landing validation and formal audit pending. Its source preparation, signed
+partial hopping, physical placement, and scheduled Born/Record events remained
+supplied. Historical instructions to open a PR and continue the campaign are
+not current actions or scientific content.
+
+The cold reviewer reconstructed the physical hopping matrices by prefix-parity
+incidence inversion, independently checked complex success/input/output columns,
+and supplied the operational two-setting witness. It identified incomplete
+original phase/amplitude assertions as a coverage gap, not a false result;
+the exact portable helper includes those stronger checks. Its fidelity lemma
+uses the witness spectrum 2, 0, 0, -2 to give F(Psi+) >= W/2 and is now explicit
+in the canonical note. The later supplement checked the specified CHSH signs,
+local commutation, permanent middle Record, and the analytic nonbridge isometry.
+The exact reviewer also performed the port; the original source disclosed that
+role overlap and distinguished root canonical review from port self-review.
+None of these historical review labels confirms new source bytes.
+
+The original scoped-boundary ledger rejected reuse of the deleted middle edge,
+identifying even failure as two output qubits, and retaining the old bridge
+parity law after adding a bypass. It explicitly asserted no universal gate,
+control or occurrence exclusion. Those boundaries and the unique fidelity
+consequence survive in the canonical source.
